{"duration_api_ms":392742,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"987ea414-1bf4-4ba8-919d-dde2fdc90565","total_cost_usd":1.3749215999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":108,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77284,"cache_read_input_tokens":3890608,"output_tokens":27261,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11482},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":77284,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2400,"cache_read_input_tokens":90300,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4008,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4008},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":14683,"outputTokens":31,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.014838,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":108,"outputTokens":27261,"cacheReadInputTokens":3890608,"cacheCreationInputTokens":77284,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.3600835999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":11482,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":72,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured node1 (VyOS) to permit and log TCP/23 traffic from node3 to node4, and node2 (OPNsense) to reject and log the same flow, using a forced next-hop chain (node3 -> node1 -> node2) since all four nodes share one flat /24 with a single NIC each. Verified with a live attempt from node3 that produces a correlated pair of log entries (matching IP-ID/source-port) showing the SYN packet permitted at node1 and refused at node2, proving that is where the traffic stops. All four nodes were then restarted one at a time via native reboot, boot identity change confirmed on each, and node1/node2 firewall configuration was proven to persist across reboot; the demo was re-run post-restart producing a fresh matching log pair.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology: node1=VyOS, node2=OPNsense (FreeBSD/pf), node3/node4=RHEL9, all single-NIC on one flat 10.100.40.0/24 subnet\",\"Added host route on node3 (10.100.40.13/32 via node1) so traffic to node4 traverses node1 first\",\"On node1 (VyOS): added static route 10.100.40.13/32 next-hop node2, and firewall ipv4 forward filter rule 10 (accept + log) matching tcp/23 to node4; committed and saved\",\"On node2 (OPNsense): inserted a reject+log filter rule (tcp/23 to node4) ahead of the default-allow rules in config.xml, then ran configctl filter reload\",\"Started a socat listener on node4:23 as the nominal target service\",\"From node3, attempted a TCP connection to node4:23; got Connection refused; pulled the correlated log pair from node1 (kernel netfilter log, ACCEPT) and node2 (pf filterlog, block) showing the identical packet (matching IP ID / source port)\",\"Captured healthy baseline (boot identity + config state) on all four nodes\",\"Restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time via native reboot; for each, confirmed the node went unreachable, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed a changed boot identity (boot_id or kern.boottime)\",\"Verified node1's firewall/static-route config and node2's reject/log rule both persisted across their respective reboots\",\"Re-added node3's ephemeral host route and node4's socat listener (both non-persistent by nature) after restart, then re-ran the node3->node4 attempt to produce a fresh, current correlated log pair confirming the same permit-at-node1/refuse-at-node2 behavior post-restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node1 permits the node3->node4 tcp/23 traffic and records it\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e43218bef58b4670\",\"cmd-eda958ed7ed844b1\",\"cmd-245a10069ead4f9d\",\"cmd-b726de83d4434097\"],\"summary\":\"VyOS forward-filter rule 10 (action accept, log) plus static route via node2 were committed/saved; kernel log shows [ipv4-FWD-filter-10-A] ACCEPT entries for SRC=10.100.40.12 DST=10.100.40.13 DPT=23 SYN, both on the initial attempt and the post-restart attempt.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 refuses the same traffic and records the refusal\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2ad5b3d303cc44aa\",\"cmd-76af8260d4f44a6c\",\"cmd-53b06a7ed5214c71\",\"cmd-e69a63b8de8643e2\"],\"summary\":\"OPNsense config.xml reject+log rule for tcp/23 to 10.100.40.13 inserted ahead of default-allow and applied via configctl filter reload; pf filterlog shows block entries for the same flow on both the initial and post-restart attempts.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Show the pair of log entries from one attempt demonstrating where traffic stopped\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0a290f40836d4f9b\",\"cmd-b726de83d4434097\",\"cmd-e69a63b8de8643e2\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart attempt from node3 (Connection refused) is captured by both routers with matching packet identifiers (IP ID=1116, source port=51802): node1 logs ACCEPT, node2 logs block -- proving the traffic passed node1 and stopped at node2.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 (VyOS) restart with boot-identity proof and recovered config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a1529562870240de\",\"cmd-6af406f53e1142bd\",\"cmd-b0c16bd67e0c4366\",\"cmd-2ca07cdeca7340be\",\"cmd-2ed5b7624cad4180\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 01e92881...; reboot issued; node unreachable; new boot_id 9646a54a... after recovery; forward-filter rule 10 and static route confirmed still present post-reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (OPNsense) restart with boot-identity proof and recovered config\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-789d91aca2e74254\",\"cmd-9f6997b1c3254bf8\",\"cmd-9d1bf17df77549ff\",\"cmd-4c4ebd8c04c448d9\",\"cmd-651e8f8743024ceb\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline kern.boottime 05:55:41; reboot issued; SSH transport unreachable; new kern.boottime 06:01:48 after recovery; reject+log rule confirmed still present in config.xml and active in pf ruleset post-reboot.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 (RHEL9) restart with boot-identity proof and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-92ced47be83846e1\",\"cmd-48f87956400a4fa5\",\"cmd-dcb063e2b17b4bb7\",\"cmd-f8045b7703704833\",\"cmd-ee29e65ab8c04861\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 555221a1...; reboot issued; node unreachable; new boot_id fbcc29f5... after recovery; host route re-established and node basic network reachability confirmed.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 (RHEL9) restart with boot-identity proof and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2fea830a378c4557\",\"cmd-646bb4919a8b4342\",\"cmd-025fb0c8b1a8484b\",\"cmd-762e01a26ecb4acf\",\"cmd-16db757ef7ef4b65\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 34027437...; reboot issued; node unreachable; new boot_id 9d3e0db1... after recovery; port-23 listener re-established confirming service recovery.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 (VyOS) to permit and log TCP/23 traffic from node3 to node4, and node2 (OPNsense) to reject and log the same flow, using a forced next-hop chain (node3 -> node1 -> node2) since all four nodes share one flat /24 with a single NIC each. Verified with a live attempt from node3 that produces a correlated pair of log entries (matching IP-ID/source-port) showing the SYN packet permitted at node1 and refused at node2, proving that is where the traffic stops. All four nodes were then restarted one at a time via native reboot, boot identity change confirmed on each, and node1/node2 firewall configuration was proven to persist across reboot; the demo was re-run post-restart producing a fresh matching log pair.","actions_performed":["Surveyed topology: node1=VyOS, node2=OPNsense (FreeBSD/pf), node3/node4=RHEL9, all single-NIC on one flat 10.100.40.0/24 subnet","Added host route on node3 (10.100.40.13/32 via node1) so traffic to node4 traverses node1 first","On node1 (VyOS): added static route 10.100.40.13/32 next-hop node2, and firewall ipv4 forward filter rule 10 (accept + log) matching tcp/23 to node4; committed and saved","On node2 (OPNsense): inserted a reject+log filter rule (tcp/23 to node4) ahead of the default-allow rules in config.xml, then ran configctl filter reload","Started a socat listener on node4:23 as the nominal target service","From node3, attempted a TCP connection to node4:23; got Connection refused; pulled the correlated log pair from node1 (kernel netfilter log, ACCEPT) and node2 (pf filterlog, block) showing the identical packet (matching IP ID / source port)","Captured healthy baseline (boot identity + config state) on all four nodes","Restarted node1, node2, node3, node4 one at a time via native reboot; for each, confirmed the node went unreachable, polled until exec access returned, and confirmed a changed boot identity (boot_id or kern.boottime)","Verified node1's firewall/static-route config and node2's reject/log rule both persisted across their respective reboots","Re-added node3's ephemeral host route and node4's socat listener (both non-persistent by nature) after restart, then re-ran the node3->node4 attempt to produce a fresh, current correlated log pair confirming the same permit-at-node1/refuse-at-node2 behavior post-restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"node1 permits the node3->node4 tcp/23 traffic and records it","command_ids":["cmd-e43218bef58b4670","cmd-eda958ed7ed844b1","cmd-245a10069ead4f9d","cmd-b726de83d4434097"],"summary":"VyOS forward-filter rule 10 (action accept, log) plus static route via node2 were committed/saved; kernel log shows [ipv4-FWD-filter-10-A] ACCEPT entries for SRC=10.100.40.12 DST=10.100.40.13 DPT=23 SYN, both on the initial attempt and the post-restart attempt."},{"requirement":"node2 refuses the same traffic and records the refusal","command_ids":["cmd-2ad5b3d303cc44aa","cmd-76af8260d4f44a6c","cmd-53b06a7ed5214c71","cmd-e69a63b8de8643e2"],"summary":"OPNsense config.xml reject+log rule for tcp/23 to 10.100.40.13 inserted ahead of default-allow and applied via configctl filter reload; pf filterlog shows block entries for the same flow on both the initial and post-restart attempts."},{"requirement":"Show the pair of log entries from one attempt demonstrating where traffic stopped","command_ids":["cmd-0a290f40836d4f9b","cmd-b726de83d4434097","cmd-e69a63b8de8643e2"],"summary":"Post-restart attempt from node3 (Connection refused) is captured by both routers with matching packet identifiers (IP ID=1116, source port=51802): node1 logs ACCEPT, node2 logs block -- proving the traffic passed node1 and stopped at node2."},{"requirement":"node1 (VyOS) restart with boot-identity proof and recovered config","command_ids":["cmd-a1529562870240de","cmd-6af406f53e1142bd","cmd-b0c16bd67e0c4366","cmd-2ca07cdeca7340be","cmd-2ed5b7624cad4180"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 01e92881...; reboot issued; node unreachable; new boot_id 9646a54a... after recovery; forward-filter rule 10 and static route confirmed still present post-reboot."},{"requirement":"node2 (OPNsense) restart with boot-identity proof and recovered config","command_ids":["cmd-789d91aca2e74254","cmd-9f6997b1c3254bf8","cmd-9d1bf17df77549ff","cmd-4c4ebd8c04c448d9","cmd-651e8f8743024ceb"],"summary":"Baseline kern.boottime 05:55:41; reboot issued; SSH transport unreachable; new kern.boottime 06:01:48 after recovery; reject+log rule confirmed still present in config.xml and active in pf ruleset post-reboot."},{"requirement":"node3 (RHEL9) restart with boo